  "summary": "I've been with the same small group my entire career. Creating, fixing and enhancing a singe, but large product. It's something that I take great pride in. Used not only to simulate real chemical/factory processes, but train new operators as well. I do everything needed: planning, designing, building, troubleshooting and testing.  I've mostly programed in C++ (and primarily a Windows service). In the last couple of years C# (service and app) has entered into the equation as well. I'm easy going and always want to find the balance of what's best for the users, product and the developers themselves.\n\nFor Fun at home:\nToo many unlabeled RaspPis; Docker swarm; more vlans than I really need; Ender 3; Windows Server/Linux/Unraid",
